## BASE MEASURES
1. 
// BASE MEASURES
Gross revenue from orders, net of the store's cut (net_usd already excludes it)
Gross Order Revenue = SUM(fact_order[net_usd])

Total refunds, net of the store's fee credit
Refunds = SUM(fact_refund[net_refund_usd])

Net revenue: what the company actually keeps
Net Revenue = [Gross Order Revenue] - [Refunds]

2.
// Gross revenue using settlement date instead of order date
Settled Revenue = 
CALCULATE(
    [Gross Order Revenue],
    USERELATIONSHIP(fact_order[settlement_date], dim_date[date])
)


3.
//  Refunds counted on the date the refund happened (Treasury's view)
Refunds Treasury = 
CALCULATE(
    [Refunds],
    USERELATIONSHIP(fact_refund[refund_date], dim_date[date])
)

4.
Net revenue credited to each studio — co-developed titles count in
// full for every studio that worked on them (per brief). CROSSFILTER opens
// the bridge->title relationship in both directions only for this measure,
// so [Net Revenue] (company total) stays unaffected by the double count.
Net Revenue by Studio = 
CALCULATE(
    [Net Revenue],
    CROSSFILTER(bridge_title_studio[title_id], dim_title[title_id], BOTH)
)

5.
// Explicit sum across studios — do NOT rely on a visual's automatic Total
// row for this measure, since CROSSFILTER can make it non-additive in
// table/matrix totals. This SUMX iterates studios one by one instead.
Sum of Studio Totals = 
SUMX(
    VALUES(dim_studio[studio_name]),
    [Net Revenue by Studio]
)

6.
Count of distinct players who placed at least one order
Paying Players = DISTINCTCOUNT(fact_order[player_id])

Average net revenue per paying player
Revenue per Paying Player = DIVIDE([Net Revenue], [Paying Players])

7.
Net revenue fixed to FY2026 Q2, regardless of page-level filters
Net Revenue FY26 Q2 = 
CALCULATE([Net Revenue], dim_date[fiscal_quarter] = "FY2026 Q2")

Net revenue fixed to FY2025 Q2, for year-over-year comparison
Net Revenue FY25 Q2 = 
CALCULATE([Net Revenue], dim_date[fiscal_quarter] = "FY2025 Q2")

Year-over-year growth, same fiscal quarter
Growth % FY26 Q2 vs FY25 Q2 = 
DIVIDE(
    [Net Revenue FY26 Q2] - [Net Revenue FY25 Q2],
    [Net Revenue FY25 Q2]
)

8.
Each title's share of its studio's total revenue.
ALL(dim_title) removes the title filter so the denominator is always
the studio's full total, not affected by which title row is showing.
% of Studio Revenue = 
DIVIDE(
    [Net Revenue by Studio],
    CALCULATE([Net Revenue by Studio], ALL(dim_title))
)

9.

10.

